config MPIPE_FS
	bool "Filesystem plugin support"
	depends on FILE_SYSTEM
	help
	  A source that reads a file in fixed-size blocks and a sink that writes
	  whatever reaches it, on any mounted Zephyr file system.

	  Neither knows what it is carrying: a file is a stream of bytes with no
	  format attached, so the source announces no capability of its own and
	  whatever follows it - typically a parser - works the format out. That
	  makes these the usual way to drive a graph without hardware.

if MPIPE_FS

config MPIPE_FS_BLOCK_SIZE
	int "Size of a buffer to read/write from/to a file"
	default 4096
	help
	  Default blocksize (read/write chunk size) used when the element blocksize
	  property is not set.
	  Also used as the size of each internal buffer when file_src falls back to
	  its own static buffer pool.

config MPIPE_FS_NUM_BUFS
	int "Number of buffers in the internal output pool"
	range 1 255
	default 1
	help
	  Number of static buffers in file_src's internal net_buf pool.
	  1 may be enough for fully synchronous pipelines; use >1 if downstream can
	  retain buffers asynchronously.
	  If downstream proposes a pool, file_src uses it instead.

endif # MPIPE_FS
